.Ed
.Pp
\fBBoth preconditions are discharged.\fP They needed a live Emacs, but a \fIbatch\fP one: the
.Ql "elisp-test"
check runs
.Ql "emacs --batch"
against the full package set, so capf dispatch and keymap state are directly assertable. \(dqNeeds a running Emacs\(dq is not the same as \(dqneeds a human at a GUI\(dq.
.Pp
What still genuinely needs eyes on a screen is narrower than the original list: whether the auto-popup delay is comfortable — which has no evidence base at all (§2.1).
The accept gesture itself is settled:
.Ql "C-M-i"
now runs
.Ql "corfu-insert"
against a
.Ql "first" Ns No "-preselected"
candidate (§2.3).
.Sh 5. EXPLICITLY OUT OF SCOPE
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
\fByasnippet migration\fP — tempel is settled.
.It
\fBAI adoption\fP — surveyed only, no recommendation (§2.6).
.It
\fBcompany-mode\fP — not evaluated; corfu is the incumbent and nothing in the research challenged it.
.It
\fBMinibuffer completion\fP (vertico/consult/orderless) — untouched.
This document covers the in-buffer side only.
.It
\fBPerformance tuning\fP — no evidence base exists (research §6.6).
Any future tuning should start by measuring, not by copying numbers.
.El
.Sh 6. ADDENDUM — \(dqLESS ANNOYING, MORE NATURAL\(dq ROUND (2026-08-26)
A second, narrow round on the in-buffer side, prompted by the request to make the popup \(dqless annoying and more natural.\(dq
It does not revisit the trigger model, the freed RET/TAB, or the capf chain — those stand.
Evidence base:
.Ql "../reviews/2026-08-completion-ux-research.7" .
Everything here is opt-out-gated per R6 and validated in
.Ql "test/completion-test.el" .
.Pp
\fB6.1 The popup no longer commits candidates you did not choose.\fP
.Ql "corfu-preview-current"
ships as
.Ql "insert" ,
which auto-inserts the selected candidate on \fIcontinued typing\fP — quietly undercutting the \(dqnever accept unless asked\(dq intent that R4 and the freed keys were built for.
Set to
.Ql "nil" :
the menu shows, nothing enters the buffer until an explicit
.Ql "corfu-insert"
.No \&( Ns Ql "C-M-i" ).
This is also what makes room for 6.4 — with corfu contributing no inline text, the ghost text is the sole inline surface.
.Pp
\fB6.2 The auto-popup timing moved onto corfu's documented defaults.\fP
.Ql "jotain-completion-auto-delay"
.Ql "0.1 → 0.2"
and
.Ql "jotain-completion-auto-prefix"
.Ql "2 → 3" .
§2.1 flagged the old
.Ql "0.1" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "2"
as unmeasured folklore; corfu's own defaults are
.Ql "0.2" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "3" ,
and its docstrings caution against sitting \fIbelow\fP them (load/flicker).
With no measurement either way, the documented resting point is the better-justified one, and
.Ql "3"
now matches
.Ql "completion-preview-minimum-symbol-length"
so both surfaces start at the same keystroke.
Still not \(dqtuned\(dq — just no longer below the values upstream warns about.
.Pp
\fB6.3 A documentation panel
.No \&( Ns Ql "corfu-popupinfo" Ns No ").\fP"
New knob
.Ql "jotain-completion-doc-popup"
(default
.Ql "t" )
enables
.Ql "corfu-popupinfo-mode" ,
the bundled IDE-style detail panel, delay
.Ql "(1.0 . 0.5)" .
It binds only
.Ql "M-t" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "M-h" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "M-g" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "C-M-v"
— no collision with the freed RET/TAB or
.Ql "M-n" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "M-p" .
.Ql "corfu-echo"
is the documented lighter fallback.
.Pp
\fB6.4 Inline ghost text
.No \&( Ns Ql "completion-preview-mode" )
— Finding 12(b), adopted.\fP New knob
.Ql "jotain-completion-inline-preview"
(default
.Ql "t" )
enables the built-in inline preview in
.Ql "jotain-completion-auto-modes"
— the \fIsame\fP mode list as the auto-popup, so prose stays quiet (R1) and the minibuffer is never touched.
It draws the top capf candidate as ghost text after point, the modern-editor feel.
.Pp
Two rule-preserving specifics, both measured in the test file:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
\fBR2 landmine, fixed.\fP
.Ql "completion-preview-active-mode-map"
binds
.Ql "C-i"
→
.Ql "completion-preview-insert" ,
and
.Ql "C-i"
\fIis\fP the TAB event — so the shipped binding is \(dqTAB accepts the preview.\(dq
.Ql "(keymap-unset … \(dqC-i\(dq t)"
removes it; TAB still only indents while a preview shows.
The whole-candidate accept moves to
.Ql "M-RET"
(R4-safe — R4 governs bare RET), and
.Ql "M-i"
(common-prefix) is left as upstream ships it.
.It
\fBR4 is safe out of the box\fP — the map binds no RET; the only obligation is not to add one.
.El
.Pp
The previewed candidate's sort is paired with
.Ql "corfu-sort-function"
(Emacs 31 user option, guarded), and the preview is inhibited inside comments/strings (Emacs 31 hook, guarded), so nothing appears where symbol completion is meaningless.
.Pp
\fB6.5 What still needs eyes on a GUI.\fP As §4 already noted for
.Ql "corfu-complete" ,
two things batch tests cannot settle: whether ghost + popup together reads as integrated or busy, and whether the prefix-only ghost (preview keeps its own
.Ql "'(basic)"
style) ever disagrees jarringly with an orderless popup row.
Both are structurally mitigated
.No \&( Ns Ql "corfu-preview-current nil" ,
matched sorts) and behind a one-line opt-out
.No \&( Ns Ql "jotain-completion-inline-preview" ).
.Pp
\fB6.6 Considered, not taken this round:\fP
.Ql "corfu-preselect 'prompt"
(marginal once auto-insert is gone), a buffer-local
.Ql "orderless-literal-only" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "basic"
style for the corfu popup (a real predictability lever, but it changes matching semantics and is orthogonal to \(dqannoying popup\(dq — deferred as its own decision), and cosmetic width-pinning.
See research §6.
.Sh 7. ADDENDUM — TAB DRIVES COMPLETION (2026-09-04)
\fBR2 is superseded on the owner's instruction.\fP The original R2 (\(dqTAB indents.
Only.\(dq) put the whole completion gesture on
.Ql "C-M-i" .
In practice
.Ql "C-M-i"
is unreliable: it is the same event as
.Ql "M-TAB"
/
.Ql "ESC TAB"
(§2.3 already recorded this), which window managers grab for Alt+Tab and which a TTY cannot tell apart — so on the affected setups the chain key never reached Emacs and completion \(dqdid not work.\(dq
The owner authorised using TAB for both indent and completion.
This addendum records that reversal; it does not revisit the trigger model (§2.1), the freed \fBRET\fP (R4 — see below), the capf chain (§2.4), or the 2026-08 UX round (§6), all of which stand.
Validated in
.Ql "test/completion-test.el" .
.Pp
\fB7.1 What R2 becomes.\fP
.Ql "tab-always-indent"
moves from
.Ql "t"
back to
.Ql "complete"
(the value §2.2 had reverted): TAB first indents the line, and once the line is already indented
.Ql "indent-for-tab-command"
runs
.Ql "completion-at-point" ,
opening the popup.
This is the standard Emacs idiom, not a fight with core.
.Pp
\fB7.2 TAB accepts inside the popup.\fP With the popup open,
.Ql "corfu-map" Ns No "'s"
.Ql "TAB"
and
.Ql "<tab>"
are repointed from corfu's default
.Ql "corfu-complete"
to
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "corfu-insert" Ns No "\fP"
— the same \(dqfinish the completion, run the
.Ql ":exit-function" ,
expand a snippet\(dq command the
.Ql "<remap> <completion-at-point>"
already used for
.Ql "C-M-i"
(§2.3).
So TAB is now the open-then-accept gesture, used twice exactly as
.Ql "C-M-i"
was, and
.Ql "C-M-i"
stays bound as the GUI-safe alternative. corfu installs
.Ql "corfu-map"
through
.Ql "overriding-terminal-local-map"
while the popup is shown, so this TAB wins over both
.Ql "indent-for-tab-command"
and completion-preview's
.Ql "C-i" .
.Pp
\fB7.3 TAB accepts the inline ghost text.\fP
.Ql "completion-preview-active-mode-map"
ships
.Ql "C-i"
(the TAB event) →
.Ql "completion-preview-insert" .
§6.4 removed it to protect R2; that removal is reversed here (rebound explicitly, not left implicit), so when only the preview shows — before the popup opens — TAB accepts the ghost text.
.Ql "M-RET"
and
.Ql "M-i"
stay as §6.4 left them.
.Pp
\fB7.4 RET is untouched — R4 stands.\fP RET remains newline-only
.No \&( Ns Ql "corfu-map"
RET unbound, the preview map binds no RET).
The owner kept R4 explicitly.
Only TAB and
.Ql "C-M-i"
accept.
.Pp
\fB7.5 One knob, one meaning,
.Ql "nil"
= stricter core.\fP
.Ql "jotain-completion-free-tab"
flips default
.Ql "t"
→
.Ql "nil" .
Its meaning is unchanged (\(dqnon-nil ⇒ TAB never completes\(dq); only the default moved, so setting it restores the whole §2.2 / 2026-08 \(dqTAB indents only\(dq behaviour —
.Ql "tab-always-indent"
.Ql "t" ,
corfu's TAB deleted, the preview's
.Ql "C-i"
deleted — in one place.
The knob remains load-time (§3.3): changing it needs a restart.
.Pp
\fB7.6 Prose.\fP
.Ql "tab-always-indent complete"
is global, so TAB also completes in prose buffers — but only as a \fImanual\fP trigger (you pressed TAB, after the line is indented), which §2.5 already licenses alongside
.Ql "C-M-i" .
R1's rule is about the \fIauto\fP-popup, which stays prog-only; nothing here makes prose pop up on its own.
